title: 'Mod playbooks, checkpoint 12: Aegis rules on naming and versioning; founder allows non-GitHub hosts and reserves brand publishers'
summary: |-
  Aegis gave APPROVE-WITH-FIXES on the naming and versioning design:
  - H1: the env prefix was ambiguous → double underscore `<PUB>__<NAME>__`.
  - H2: legacy modns overlap → only alias-table mods keep legacy kinds.
  - H3: MCP server hash collision → hash10 plus COLLISION refusal at install and load.
  - M items: an upgradedHash on the grant; no fresh v1 installs; canonical git URLs with followRedirects=false; downgrade decided by packageHash history; folder-replaces-git gets a full card; principal labels and row schema carry the publisher.

  Founder rulings:
  (1) Non-GitHub git hosts ARE allowed in 8.0, overriding Aegis's github-only recommendation. Implemented as publisher identity (host, namespace), a root-signed TOFU grant.publisher binding, and display "acme @ gitlab.com".
  (2) github.com/a-company is owned by an unrelated person, so `a-company` is refused from every source.
  (3) Reserved publishers: ascend42 (github owner only), warpline, nevr, nevrland, conductor, constellation, neurons.

  The consolidated spec is in .paradigm/research/paradigm-8/gnomon-mod-naming-versioning.md and lands as S0b on feat/gnomon-desk-o1.
